  <entry>
    <title>Writing Effective Copilot Instructions for Complex Codebases</title>
    <link href="https://endjin.com/blog/writing-effective-copilot-instructions-for-complex-codebases"/>
    <id>urn:uuid:1225c695-cfb8-4ebb-aaaa-80da344efa6c</id>
    <published>2026-08-07T11:30:00Z</published>
    <updated>2026-08-07T12:00:00Z</updated>
    <summary>Modular skill files beat one monolithic instructions document once a repository stops fitting in context.</summary>
    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Guidance for an AI assistant is <strong>documentation with a consumer</strong>, and it rots the same way.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Split by task, not by subsystem</li>
          <li>Say what the build gate actually checks</li>
          <li>Record the reasoning, not just the rule</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </content>
    <category term="developer-experience" scheme="https://endjin.com/tags" label="Developer Experience"/>
  </entry>

